=2 Walkthrough
* You cannot start this quest if you have another {q:Weapon Skill Quest|WSNM|Weapon Skill Quest} active. You must return to the person that gave said quest and quit it to start another.
* Speaking with {n:Jakoh Wahcondalo} (J-9, house next to the HP) will grant you the {@k} {k:Weapons Training Guide|Weapon training guide} as well as the {p:Dagger of Trials}. You will need to break the latent on the {p:Dagger of Trials} before completing the rest of the quest.

:* Breaking the Latent

::* With the {p:Dagger of Trials} equipped in your Main hand, fight experience-yielding mobs ("Incredibly Easy Prey" or higher) and perform {p:Weapon Skills|Category:Weapon Skills} or close {p:Skillchains|Category:Skillchain} to accumulate 300 "Trial Points".

|^Skillchain Level|Points
|No Skillchain|5
|Level 1|7
|Level 2|9
|Level 3|11

::* You know you have enough points when the latent breaks. You will know it is done when the weapon's elemental resistances disappear from your active resistances (colored dots below the gear grid, but above the selected item description). **The item's description text will never change**.

!Broken Latent.png||
* Trade the {p:Dagger of Trials} back to {n:Jakoh Wahcondalo}. This will give you the {@k} {k:Map to the Annals of Truth}. You will be instructed to travel to {z:Gustav Tunnel}.
** The quickest way to the NM is the level 128 unity warp. This will put right inside the tunnel that's leading to the NM. You will also find a Grounds Tome close to your spawn point where you can get Sneak and Invisible.
* Take {i:Silent Oils|Silent Oil|4165} and {i:Prism Powders|Prism Powder|4164} with you and head to {z:Gustav Tunnel}. Once inside, follow the path to (G-9) and take the western tunnel. At the fork in this tunnel, head east. In the large room, take the eastern tunnel at (I-8). The ??? to spawn the NM is at (I-9) Map 2.

=4 From the Unity Warp Level 128
* Head north and hug the east wall.
* The spawn is near the intersection of (I-9) and (J-9)

* This fight is against {m:Baronial Bat}. It is weak to {p:Wind} and {p:Light} attacks. Once you kill it, re-examine the ??? to receive the {@k} {k:Annals of Truth}.

* Go back and speak with {n:Jakoh Wahcondalo} to receive your reward.

